def H(code, d, q, right, wrong, e): return B.hand(code, d, q, right, wrong, e)

H("872.d.1.A",3,"A student arranges to run a small inventory-counting project at a distribution center: she sets goals, schedules her weeks, completes the counts and reviews how it went. She is:","planning, conducting and evaluating an industry-based occupational experience",["only watching others","skipping the review","doing the work at random"],"A supervised experience follows plan, do, evaluate.")
H("872.d.1.A",4,"A written proposal for a supervised warehouse project should be reviewed and approved by:","the teacher and the work-site supervisor before work begins",["no one","only classmates","the delivery driver"],"Approval keeps the project aligned.")
H("872.d.1.B",3,"A student writes down each pallet count, the shift and the supervisor's initials on a daily log for her warehouse project. She is applying:","proper record-keeping skills",["storage tricks","random notes","guessing skills"],"Daily logs document work.")
H("872.d.1.B",4,"Which entry makes the best record of a logistics learning activity?","date, hours, task performed, result and supervisor signature",["only a smiley face","no date","only the weather"],"Complete records include key facts.")
H("872.d.1.C",3,"A student sets up a tracker with tabs for orders picked, errors found and hours worked for her warehouse job. She is:","using a customized record-keeping system for her industry experience",["using no system","using a generic note only","copying a template unchanged"],"Custom systems track what matters.")
H("872.d.1.C",4,"A record system for an order-picking project is most helpful if it:","tracks accuracy and speed over time",["has no dates","tracks unrelated hobbies","is never opened"],"Track measures that show progress.")
H("872.d.1.D",3,"A student runs a food-drive collection with her logistics club and coordinates volunteers to sort and ship the boxes. This is an example of:","a youth leadership opportunity",["a payroll task","a vehicle repair","a customs fine"],"Leading a project builds leadership.")
H("872.d.1.D",4,"How does serving as a team captain for a student supply-chain contest help a student's work experience?","it builds communication, planning and leadership skills",["it replaces the work","it avoids responsibility","it limits growth"],"Roles build skills.")
H("872.d.1.E",3,"Before starting a job-shadowing project, a student lists the weekly tasks, the supplies she needs and the costs of transportation. She is developing:","a work plan and budget",["a travel photo album","a menu","a floor plan"],"Plans include tasks and costs.")
H("872.d.1.E",4,"If a project's expected expenses are $120 and the student has $90, the budget shows:","a $30 shortfall that needs a plan",["a $30 surplus","no difference","a $210 total income"],"120 − 90 = 30.")
H("872.d.2.A",3,"A student notices that some countries use pallets of different standard sizes than the United States. This is a:","difference in international practices in distribution",["similarity in every nation","mistake in measurement","rule for pilots"],"Standards differ internationally.")
H("872.d.2.A",4,"A similarity between warehouses in different nations is that most:","store goods, track inventory and move orders out",["avoid shipping","use no systems","sell directly to customers only"],"Basic functions are shared.")
H("872.d.2.B",3,"A distributor sells medical gloves to Canada, auto parts to Mexico and grain to Egypt. This shows:","the variety of world markets",["only a local market","no demand","limited trade"],"Different markets want different goods.")
H("872.d.2.B",4,"Before expanding a delivery service overseas, a company should study the:","needs, rules and income levels of the new market",["color of the trucks","menu of a café","name of the mayor only"],"Research the market first.")
H("872.d.2.C",3,"A logistics manager learns that package labels must be translated and that one country's customers prefer cash on delivery. These are:","marketing factors and practices that affect other cultures",["engine repairs","road hazards","office supplies"],"Local practices shape marketing.")
H("872.d.2.C",4,"A brand name that sounds fine in English but has a negative meaning abroad shows why companies must:","research language and culture before marketing",["avoid labels","use the same ad everywhere","skip testing"],"Cultural research prevents blunders.")
H("872.d.3.A",3,"A new warehouse hire learns that 'SKU' is a unique code for each product and 'cross-docking' means moving goods straight from inbound to outbound trucks. She is:","learning terms used in distribution and logistics",["avoiding vocabulary","guessing words","skipping orientation"],"Know the terms.")
H("872.d.3.A",4,"In logistics, 'lead time' is:","the time between placing an order and receiving it",["the length of a pallet","a type of truck","a forklift attachment"],"Lead time measures order-to-receipt delay.")
H("872.d.3.B",3,"Online orders reach homes in two days because of fulfillment centers and delivery networks. This shows the:","scope and effect of distribution and logistics on society",["limited role of logistics","small impact","absence of trade"],"Logistics shapes daily life.")
H("872.d.3.B",4,"If a regional distribution center shut down unexpectedly, nearby stores would most likely:","run short of stock and lose sales",["receive extra stock","have no change","lower all prices"],"Supply chain disruptions cause shortages.")
H("872.d.3.C",3,"The adoption of barcodes, containerization and online order tracking are examples of:","significant historical and current developments in logistics",["fictional ideas","unrelated hobbies","minor changes"],"Technology reshaped logistics.")
H("872.d.3.C",4,"Which current development lets customers see a package's location in real time?","GPS and scan-based tracking",["a handwritten ledger","a rotary phone","a paper map only"],"Tracking uses scans and GPS.")
H("872.d.3.D",3,"Engineers testing warehouse robots that pick and sort items and delivery drones are exploring:","possible future scenarios for distribution and logistics",["historical events","unrelated sports","old methods"],"Prototypes hint at the future.")
H("872.d.3.D",4,"A likely future scenario in large fulfillment centers is:","more automation with robots working alongside people",["no technology","fewer products","a return to paper only"],"Automation is expanding.")
H("872.d.3.E",3,"A retailer uses artificial intelligence to forecast demand and ships goods from overseas factories on tight schedules. This shows how:","emerging technologies and globalization affect distribution",["technology has no role","globalization lowers trade","forecasts slow orders"],"Technology and global trade work together.")
H("872.d.3.E",4,"Global supply chains make companies more vulnerable to:","disruptions at faraway ports or suppliers",["local weather only","nothing at all","local holidays only"],"Long chains have more risk points.")
H("872.d.3.F",3,"A company weighs paying more for faster air freight against cheaper but slower ocean shipping. This is comparing:","issues affecting logistics such as cost, speed and reliability",["only colors","only holidays","only uniforms"],"Trade-offs shape shipping choices.")
H("872.d.3.F",4,"A big factor driving up the cost of last-mile delivery in cities is:","traffic congestion and failed delivery attempts",["short routes","low fuel use","empty roads"],"Last-mile costs are high.")
H("872.d.4.A",3,"A warehouse manager forecasts demand, assigns staff, tracks budgets and checks results against targets. These are:","common business management principles",["random acts","personal chores","hobbies"],"Plan, organize, lead, control.")
H("872.d.4.A",4,"A manager who compares shipping errors against the goal and fixes the process is using the function of:","controlling",["avoiding","delaying","guessing"],"Controlling compares results to goals.")
H("872.d.4.B",3,"A forklift operator signs up for a supervisor-in-training course and mentors new hires. She is:","taking an opportunity for leadership development and personal growth",["avoiding promotion","ignoring training","quitting"],"Training builds leaders.")
H("872.d.4.B",4,"Which activity best develops leadership in a distribution career?","leading a safety huddle at the start of a shift",["working in silence","skipping meetings","avoiding feedback"],"Leading huddles builds leadership.")
H("872.d.4.C",3,"A student council chair posts an agenda, recognizes speakers and calls for a vote on each motion. She is demonstrating:","democratic principles in conducting an effective meeting",["unfair control","avoiding discussion","random talk"],"Fair procedures.")
H("872.d.4.C",4,"Which job belongs to the secretary at a formal meeting?","recording the minutes of what was decided",["running the vote count only","owning the gavel","setting the agenda alone"],"The secretary keeps minutes.")
H("872.d.4.D",3,"A shift team of pickers, packers and loaders handles a holiday rush with clear roles and open communication. This shows strong:","team dynamics",["isolation","competition only","confusion"],"Healthy teams share roles and communicate.")
H("872.d.4.D",4,"One stage that a new team often goes through as members test roles and ideas is called:","storming",["ending","sleeping","hiding"],"Tuckman's storming stage.")
H("872.d.4.E",3,"A logistics company says it aims to deliver every order accurately and on time and sets a goal of 99 percent order accuracy. This is:","developing an organizational vision, mission and goals",["setting no direction","ignoring customers","a random statement"],"Goals follow from the mission.")
H("872.d.4.E",4,"A measurable organizational goal is:","reduce average order processing time from 48 hours to 36 hours this year",["be better","work hard","improve someday"],"Measurable goals include numbers and a time.")
H("872.d.5.A",3,"A warehouse in Laredo handles shipments between Texas and Mexico because each side makes goods the other wants at lower cost. This explains a reason for:","world trade and globalization",["isolation","price fixing","trade bans"],"Trade rewards specialization.")
H("872.d.5.A",4,"Which factor most encourages two countries to trade electronics and produce?","each produces something the other values more cheaply",["identical economies","no ports","no demand"],"Comparative advantage.")
H("872.d.5.B",3,"Lawmakers debate whether to fund a new inland port, and local businesses and residents argue over the plan. This shows the:","political impact of distribution and logistics",["absence of politics","lack of interest","random events"],"Logistics projects involve politics.")
H("872.d.5.B",4,"Tariffs on imported goods affect logistics companies because they:","change shipping volumes and costs",["remove all risk","end shipping","make trucks faster"],"Trade policy affects flows.")
H("872.d.5.C",3,"A distribution center reviews customs and hazardous-materials shipping rules and updates its labeling procedures. This is:","reviewing regulations and laws to evaluate their impact on operations",["avoiding laws","ignoring updates","skipping training"],"Stay compliant.")
H("872.d.5.C",4,"Failing to follow hazardous-materials shipping rules could lead a company to face:","fines, accidents and loss of shipping privileges",["lower insurance","higher bonuses","no consequence"],"Noncompliance has penalties.")
H("872.d.5.D",3,"A logistics supervisor reads a supply chain newsletter each week to track port delays and fuel trends. This shows:","reading written material to stay abreast of current issues",["avoiding news","ignoring trends","skipping reading"],"Stay informed.")
H("872.d.5.D",4,"Reading industry reports can help a distribution manager to:","anticipate changes that affect inventory and routes",["avoid forecasts","skip training","ignore customers"],"Awareness supports planning.")
H("872.d.5.E",3,"A distribution company polls its retail customers about delivery times and tallies late-order complaints before changing routes. It is:","collecting public opinion and data to make informed decisions",["guessing","ignoring customers","avoiding data"],"Gather feedback and data.")
H("872.d.5.E",4,"The strongest basis for deciding to add a second shift is:","order backlog data and customer lead-time surveys",["a single opinion","a rumor","a hunch"],"Data supports decisions.")
H("872.d.5.F",3,"A logistics planner lists three warehouse sites, compares the cost, travel time and storage capacity of each, and recommends one. She is using:","critical-thinking skills to identify and organize alternatives",["random picks","copying competitors","avoiding options"],"Compare alternatives.")
H("872.d.5.F",4,"After listing alternatives for reducing late deliveries, the next step is to:","weigh each option against cost, time and risk",["choose the first one","ignore costs","stop planning"],"Evaluate each option.")
H("872.d.5.G",3,"A retailer checks whether its third-party carrier delivered 97 percent of orders on time as agreed in the contract. This is:","evaluating performance and contract compliance of service providers",["ignoring the contract","paying blindly","avoiding records"],"Review providers against agreements.")
H("872.d.5.G",4,"If a carrier repeatedly damages goods in transit despite contract terms, the company should:","document the damage and enforce or renegotiate the contract",["ignore it","pay a bonus","hide the claims"],"Hold providers accountable.")
H("872.d.6.A",3,"A shipping clerk is told to change the weight on a form to lower the freight charge. She refuses because it would be dishonest and illegal. She is examining:","workplace ethical and legal responsibilities",["pay rates","dress codes","break times"],"Honesty and law guide conduct.")
H("872.d.6.A",4,"Which behavior best reflects ethical responsibility for someone who handles customer shipments?","reporting a damaged or missing item truthfully",["hiding the damage","blaming a customer","skipping the report"],"Honesty protects trust.")
H("872.d.6.B",3,"A customer service rep thanks callers, uses names politely and waits for them to finish speaking. She is using:","proper etiquette",["rude habits","slang only","interruptions"],"Courtesy matters.")
H("872.d.6.B",4,"Good etiquette when emailing a client about a delayed shipment includes:","a clear subject line, polite tone and proposed next steps",["all capital letters","insults","no greeting"],"Professional email etiquette.")
H("872.d.6.C",3,"A warehouse associate arrives with clean clothes, closed-toe shoes and enough sleep before a long shift. This shows:","appropriate personal appearance and health habits",["poor grooming","ignoring rest","careless dress"],"Appearance and health habits matter.")
H("872.d.6.C",4,"Staying hydrated and taking scheduled breaks helps a warehouse worker by:","keeping energy and focus high while lifting and moving goods",["increasing errors","slowing workflow only","raising injury risk"],"Health supports safety.")
H("872.d.6.D",3,"A dispatcher writes a short email to a carrier about a changed pickup time and then calls the driver to confirm. She is practicing:","written and oral communication in formal and informal situations",["silence only","confusion","avoidance"],"Combine writing and talking.")
H("872.d.6.D",4,"A message to a carrier about a late pickup is clearest when it states:","the order number, the new time and the location",["only an apology","no details","a joke"],"Include key facts.")
H("872.d.6.E",3,"A dock supervisor listens during the morning meeting, writes down the changes to the loading schedule and asks a question about door assignments. She is:","practicing effective listening skills",["ignoring directions","distracted listening","interrupting"],"Active listening includes notes and questions.")
H("872.d.6.E",4,"The best way to confirm that a caller's complaint has been understood is to:","restate the complaint in your own words and ask if it is right",["interrupt","say 'whatever'","end the call"],"Paraphrase to confirm.")
H("872.d.6.F",3,"A student uses a warehouse manual to write step-by-step instructions for receiving a pallet. She is:","employing writing and preparation skills with technical information",["guessing steps","copying jokes","skipping details"],"Technical writing is precise.")
H("872.d.6.F",4,"A well-written receiving procedure should list steps:","in the order they must be done, with safety warnings",["in random order","without warnings","as a paragraph with no breaks"],"Order and warnings matter.")
H("872.d.6.G",3,"A student explains to the class how a pick-to-light system speeds up order filling, using a poster and a steady voice. He is demonstrating:","speaking skills",["silence","mumbling","reading silently"],"Present clearly.")
H("872.d.6.G",4,"To make a short technical talk more engaging, a speaker should:","use a visual aid and keep the key points brief",["read every word","speak in a monotone","avoid the audience"],"Visuals and brevity help.")
H("872.d.7.A",3,"A logistics firm funds work on faster sorting algorithms, better packaging materials and electric delivery vans. These are:","major fields of research and development",["unrelated hobbies","decorations","payroll tasks"],"R&D spans many fields.")
H("872.d.7.A",4,"Research and development in distribution tends to focus on:","lowering costs, speeding delivery and reducing waste",["adding delays","raising errors","skipping safety"],"R&D improves performance.")
H("872.d.7.B",3,"A team asks whether a new pallet-wrap pattern reduces load shifting, tests it on 20 shipments and compares results with the old pattern. They are:","applying scientific methods of research",["guessing","copying","ignoring data"],"Test, record, compare.")
H("872.d.7.B",4,"For a fair comparison of two packing methods, the team should:","use the same products and routes for both methods",["use different products for each","change many things","test once only"],"Control variables.")
H("872.d.7.C",3,"A student researching conveyor safety consults an equipment manual, a trade association report and a safety officer. She is:","using a variety of resources for research and development",["using one source","using none","guessing"],"Use varied sources.")
H("872.d.7.C",4,"The best source for current federal workplace safety data is:","an official government agency such as OSHA",["an anonymous blog","a rumor","a social media comment"],"Official sources are reliable.")
H("872.d.7.D",3,"A researcher states a hypothesis, designs a test, collects data, analyzes it and reports results. This sequence describes:","the scientific method of research",["a sales pitch","a rumor","a guess"],"Follow the method.")
H("872.d.7.D",4,"After testing, if the data does not support the hypothesis, a researcher should:","revise the hypothesis or design a new test",["hide the data","change the data","ignore the result"],"Science follows evidence.")
H("872.d.8.A",3,"A student proposes adding barcode scanners at the receiving dock, outlining the problem, cost and expected time savings for a manager. She is:","discussing a project proposal",["avoiding ideas","skipping planning","ignoring costs"],"Proposals outline problem, cost and benefit.")
H("872.d.8.A",4,"The part of a proposal that persuades decision makers by showing what the company gains is the:","expected benefit",["title page only","signature line","page number"],"Benefits justify cost.")
H("872.d.8.B",3,"A receiving clerk logs each shipment's arrival time, carrier, count and condition in the warehouse system. This is:","maintaining records appropriate to distribution and logistics",["hiding data","skipping paperwork","losing data"],"Receiving records are required.")
H("872.d.8.B",4,"Accurate receiving records help a company to:","resolve damage claims and keep inventory correct",["avoid inspections","hide shortages","skip counts"],"Records support claims.")
H("872.d.8.C",3,"A planner records daily orders shipped for a month in a table and plots them on a line graph. She is:","collecting and organizing data in tables and graphs",["hiding numbers","guessing","avoiding data"],"Tables and graphs organize data.")
H("872.d.8.C",4,"Which chart type best shows the share of shipments by carrier?","a pie chart",["a blank page","a paragraph only","a map of the parking lot"],"Pie charts show parts of a whole.")
H("872.d.8.D",3,"A chart shows damaged shipments dropped from 12 to 4 per month after a new packing method. An analyst concludes:","the new method likely reduced damage, though more data would confirm it",["nothing changed","damage rose","data is meaningless"],"Interpret trends with caution.")
H("872.d.8.D",4,"A graph shows weekly orders of 500, 520, 510, 150 and 505. The 150 is best described as:","an unusual value to investigate",["a typical week","the average","an error to delete always"],"Check outliers.")
H("872.d.9.A",3,"A planner uses warehouse management software to assign storage locations, emails carriers pickup times and checks a port website for delays. These are:","management, email and Internet applications in logistics",["unrelated tools","hand tools","office furniture"],"Software supports operations.")
H("872.d.9.A",4,"A warehouse management system helps a facility to:","track inventory locations and guide picking efficiently",["increase misplaced items","hide stock levels","slow shipping"],"WMS tracks and directs.")
H("872.d.9.B",3,"A clerk writes a procedure, tracks stock counts in a spreadsheet, stores supplier details in a database and builds slides for a training. She is using:","word-processing, database, spreadsheet and presentation software",["only a calculator","no software","only paper"],"Office software types.")
H("872.d.9.B",4,"The best tool for storing thousands of customer records with searchable fields is a:","database",["slide deck","word document","photo album"],"Databases store and search records.")
H("872.d.9.C",3,"Teams in Dallas and Memphis review a shared inventory plan on a video call and edit the same file at once. These tools are:","collaborative, groupware and virtual meeting software",["isolated tools","paper tools","hand tools"],"Collaboration software connects teams.")
H("872.d.9.C",4,"Groupware helps a distribution team because it:","lets members share files and update plans together",["blocks communication","prevents editing","limits sharing"],"Groupware supports teamwork.")
H("872.d.9.D",3,"A fleet manager studies a map showing delivery clusters and uses satellite signals to track her trucks. These are:","Geographic Information Systems and Global Positioning Systems",["hand drawings","weather reports only","guesswork"],"GIS maps data; GPS locates vehicles.")
H("872.d.9.D",4,"A GIS is most useful to a logistics planner for:","choosing warehouse locations near customers and good roads",["painting a sign","naming a product","hiring a driver"],"GIS supports location decisions.")
H("872.d.9.E",3,"A distribution center uses handheld scanners, barcode printers and conveyor controls tied to its software. These are:","other computer-based equipment in distribution and logistics",["unrelated devices","office furniture","hand tools only"],"Scanners and controls are computer-based equipment.")
H("872.d.9.E",4,"Scanning a barcode at receiving helps a warehouse by:","recording the item automatically and reducing errors",["adding errors","slowing receiving","removing records"],"Scanning improves accuracy.")
H("872.d.10.A",3,"At the start of a shift, a warehouse team reviews the evacuation routes, the location of extinguishers and safe lifting methods. They are discussing:","safe work practices and emergency procedures",["break schedules","pay rates","parking rules"],"Safety briefings cover practices and emergencies.")
H("872.d.10.A",4,"If a fire alarm sounds in a warehouse, workers should first:","stop work and follow the evacuation plan to the assembly point",["finish the task","hide","wait for orders to ignore it"],"Evacuate promptly.")
H("872.d.10.B",3,"Rules from OSHA, such as requirements for forklift training and guarding, are examples of:","laws designed to promote safety and health in distribution workplaces",["optional tips","marketing slogans","rumors"],"OSHA sets workplace rules.")
H("872.d.10.B",4,"Under OSHA rules, employers must train forklift operators:","before they operate the equipment",["after an accident","never","only once a decade"],"Training must come first.")
H("872.d.10.C",3,"A trainee practices a pressure bandage on a mannequin arm and performs chest compressions on a manikin. He is demonstrating:","first aid and CPR procedures",["office tasks","cleaning","parking"],"Emergency response skills.")
H("872.d.10.C",4,"If a coworker collapses and does not respond or breathe normally, the first action is to:","call 911 or direct someone to, and begin compressions if trained",["wait for a break","give a drink","leave the area"],"Call and begin compressions.")
H("872.d.10.D",3,"A dock worker wears steel-toe boots, gloves and a high-visibility vest while loading trucks. She is demonstrating:","proper use of safety equipment",["ignoring rules","fashion choices","unsafe dress"],"Wear required PPE.")
H("872.d.10.D",4,"A back-support belt or proper lifting posture is used to help reduce the risk of:","strain injuries while moving heavy goods",["eye damage","hearing loss","sunburn"],"Lifting safely prevents strains.")
H("872.d.11.A",3,"A receiving team learns to stack boxes with heavy items on the bottom, keep fragile goods on top and use gloves with sharp edges. They are discussing:","handling practices for goods and materials",["dress codes","pay practices","parking rules"],"Handling affects damage and safety.")
H("872.d.11.A",4,"Goods marked 'this side up' should be:","kept upright during handling and storage",["turned over","stacked sideways","dropped"],"Follow handling labels.")
H("872.d.11.B",3,"A shipper checks that a box's dimensions and weight fit a carrier's limits before sending it. She is explaining:","size, weight and shape requirements for packaging",["parking limits","color choices","pay scales"],"Carriers set size and weight rules.")
H("872.d.11.B",4,"A package that exceeds a carrier's weight limit may be:","refused or charged extra fees",["delivered free","sent faster","ignored"],"Oversize costs more.")
H("872.d.11.C",3,"A shop chooses pallets and racks for storage, a forklift for moving goods and a parcel carrier for delivery. These are:","material handling, storage and shipping methods",["decorating choices","pay rates","parking choices"],"Methods for handling, storage and shipping.")
H("872.d.11.C",4,"Which shipping method is usually best for fast delivery of a small, urgent package?","express air freight",["slow barge","bulk rail","hand cart"],"Air is fastest.")
H("872.d.11.D",3,"A designer checks that the box is clear, readable and shows the barcode, the handling marks and the brand logo in the right places. She is:","analyzing visual design and appearance requirements for packages",["avoiding labels","hiding information","guessing"],"Packages must be readable and compliant.")
H("872.d.11.D",4,"An important appearance requirement for a package label is that it be:","legible and placed where scanners can read it",["small and faded","hidden","covered by tape"],"Legible labels prevent misrouting.")
H("872.d.11.E",3,"A supervisor sketches the path packages will take from the receiving dock through sorting, packing and shipping to reduce travel. She is discussing:","layout plans for processing packages",["a menu","a vacation list","a parking plan only"],"Layouts affect flow.")
H("872.d.11.E",4,"A good layout for a packing area should:","minimize backtracking and keep the work flowing in one direction",["maximize walking","cross paths often","block exits"],"Smooth flow saves time.")
H("872.d.11.F",3,"A team compares pallet jacks, conveyors, dock levelers and racking systems used to move and store goods. They are identifying:","material handling and storage equipment",["office furniture","decorations","hand tools only"],"Equipment moves and stores goods.")
H("872.d.11.F",4,"A device that bridges the gap between a dock and a truck bed so forklifts can drive on is a:","dock leveler",["pallet label","scanner","rack beam"],"Dock levelers bridge height gaps.")
H("872.d.11.G",3,"A company runs a large central facility that gathers goods from many suppliers and ships them to stores in a region. This is a:","distribution center",["retail store","office tower","farm"],"Distribution centers serve many stores.")
H("872.d.11.G",4,"A facility with temperature control for storing goods such as vaccines and produce is a:","cold storage warehouse",["parking garage","open-air lot","gift shop"],"Cold storage keeps goods cool.")

